[posix] mincore (CBF2b) answers from the kernel's count of present pages in each mapping: exact for a mapping with all or none of its pages present, a guess between (the first resident pages of the mapping), so a test that asks about one page of a part-resident mapping fails (CheckPageInCore says false for a page that is there; the heap profiler's resident_total reads 0). 12 of the 21 pass (the other Purge* tests, ProcessMemoryDumpTest.CountResidentBytes*). Needs the per-page kernel query: CR-PLAN, "CBF2b notes", decision 1
