[proc] ModuleCacheTest.CheckAgainstProcMaps wants two modules (this one and ld-linux.so) and a static program has one: by design. SmapsRollupTest.ReadAndParse needs /proc/self/smaps_rollup, which CBF4 did not build; the test skipped itself while uname said 0.1.0 and runs since CBF2b's 5.10.0-jamos (the program aborts on an empty optional). The other 13 /proc tests pass (CBF4)
ModuleCacheTest.CheckAgainstProcMaps
SmapsRollupTest.ReadAndParse

