PersistentMemoryAllocatorTest.TruncateTest

[toolchain] PartitionAlloc reserves the low 4 GiB (a PROT_NONE zero segment, from 64 KiB, its own constant: nothing is read from the OS) as one mapping, and the program's image sits at 0x400000 in the way, so it keeps the 64 KiB it assumes (the layer also ignores an mmap address hint: CR-PLAN, "CBF2b notes"). ZeroSegmentInaccessibleEnd reads the segment's last byte and expects to die: nothing is reserved there ("failed to die"; the Begin test passes)
PartitionAddressSpaceTest.ZeroSegment
PartitionAddressSpaceTest.ZeroSegmentInaccessibleEnd
